    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="1078" n="927" xml:id="pg927"/>

                <head>258. Memorandum from Kaysen to Gen.
                        Taylor, January 23<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d258-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline><date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1962-01-23">January 23,
                        1962</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d258-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d258-1"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Ltr to SecDef 1/22/62 (S)</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President sent your memorandum to the Secretary and also called him. Judging
                    from my side of the conversation, the Secretary has shown no great increase in
                    his receptivity to this idea. The President indicated he would like McNamara to talk to you and Bell. I am sending a copy of your memorandum
                    to Bell.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_KC_1">Carl
                        Kaysen</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d258-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d258-f1-content">
                <p>Relays President’s interest in having Taylor talk with McNamara. No classification marking. 1 p. Kennedy Library,
                    National Security Files, Departments and Agencies Series, DOD 1/62–3/62.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
